<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title><%= title %></title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
<nav class="navbar">
  <strong>🟢 Exp 12 – Node.js + Express + EJS</strong>
  <a href="/">Home</a>
  <a href="/form">Form</a>
  <a href="/students">Students</a>
  <a href="/about">About</a>
</nav>
<div class="container">
  <div class="card">
    <h1>🚀 <%= title %></h1>
    <p>Built by <strong><%= author %></strong> | UPES Backend Development Lab | <%= year %></p>
    <p>This page is rendered by <strong>EJS</strong> (Embedded JavaScript) template engine via <code>res.render()</code>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>📋 Available Routes</h2>
    <p>Click any route to test it. All responses are live from the Express server.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Route</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <% routes.forEach((r, i) => { %>
        <tr>
          <td><%= i + 1 %></td>
          <td><a href="<%= r.path %>"><code><%= r.path %></code></a></td>
          <td><%= r.desc %></td>
        </tr>
        <% }) %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>📦 What is EJS?</h2>
    <p><strong>EJS (Embedded JavaScript)</strong> lets you embed JS directly in HTML templates using special tags:</p>
    <pre>
&lt;% code here %&gt;       — executes JS (no output)
&lt;%= expression %&gt;     — outputs escaped HTML
&lt;%- html %&gt;           — outputs unescaped HTML
&lt;% if (x) { %&gt; ... &lt;% } %&gt;   — conditionals
&lt;% items.forEach(i => { %&gt; ... &lt;% }) %&gt;  — loops
    </pre>
  </div>
</div>
<footer>&copy; <%= year %> Satyam Koranga – Exp 12: Node.js, NPM, Express, Nodemon, EJS</footer>
</body>
</html>
